# Supply chain attack mitigation: delay installing newly published packages.
# 7-day cooldown blocks ~80% of attacks (8/10 in Woodruff's analysis had
# windows < 7 days). 14 days would block ~90%, but delays security patches.
# See: https://blog.yossarian.net/2025/11/21/We-should-all-be-using-dependency-cooldowns
min-release-age=7

# GitHub Packages (npm.pkg.github.com)
# Private packages require a token with `read:packages`.
# Only the variable name lives here so this file can be committed;
# the value is exported from `gh auth token` in config.fish at shell startup.
# pnpm aborts with "Failed to replace env in config" if the variable is unset.
//npm.pkg.github.com/:_authToken=${GITHUB_PACKAGES_TOKEN}
